# Mallowtick: Caddy in front of the Next.js web app. See docs/deploy.md.
#
# Browsers reach Caddy directly (this PC, or a VM). Caddy trusts no proxy in
# front of it, so the client is the TCP peer, and any X-Forwarded-For the
# client sends is thrown away. The web app's /api/v1 proxy route forwards the
# header to the API, which trusts it only from the web container
# (TRUSTED_PROXIES in docker-compose.yml) and limits each client by it.
#
# With a Cloudflare tunnel in front, use Caddyfile.tunnel instead
# (deploy/compose.tunnel.yml switches to it).

# SITE_ADDRESS (docker-compose.yml) is ":80" for plain HTTP on any host name,
# or a domain such as mallowtick.duckdns.org for automatic HTTPS.
{$SITE_ADDRESS::80} {
	reverse_proxy web:3000 {
		# Exactly one address: the client as Caddy resolved it.
		header_up X-Forwarded-For {client_ip}
	}
	log
}
